.TH PERITUS 1 "September 2026" "Peritus" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
peritus \- local-first coding agent with a supervised per-user daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peritus
.RI [ command " " arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Peritus starts an interactive terminal coding workspace when invoked without a
command. It discovers or creates per-user application state, starts or reuses its
matching daemon, and opens the terminal interface. It does not require a system
service or a root-owned background process.
.PP
Use
.B peritus help
for the complete command interface and the arguments supported by this version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed command version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print command usage.
.SH UPDATES
When installed from a Debian or RPM package, Peritus does not download or install
self-updates. Install a newer signed package with the system package manager.
Archive installations have a separate
.B peritus update
command and cached startup update checks.
.SH SECURITY
Run Peritus as your ordinary login user. Linux task execution requires the
supported Landlock, seccomp, and user-namespace facilities. Provider credentials
require an unlocked session credential store. Installing this package does not
create provider accounts, grant credentials, or disable host security policy.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/lib/peritus/
Matching command, daemon, terminal interface, and sandbox-helper binaries.
.TP
.B /usr/share/doc/peritus/
Product documentation; Debian packages also store copyright and license notices here.
.TP
.B /usr/share/licenses/peritus/
Copyright and third-party license notices in RPM installations.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR dnf (8),
.BR gpg (1)
.PP
https://github.com/Corvidae-Coding-Projects/Project-Peritus
